### What advisory means

Every guard was installed **advisory-first**: hooks warn (or ask, on a real
secret-scan finding) instead of denying, and each CI job carries
`continue-on-error: true`, so nothing blocks a commit or a PR yet. Advisory is
a decision-verb difference only — the detection predicates are identical to
enforcement mode.

### Promoting a guard to enforcement (one line per surface)

Promote only after **at least one observed clean advisory run** — a gate that
has never run green is a wall, not a floor.

- Hooks (`.claude/hooks/<guard>.sh`): change `MODE="advisory"` to `MODE="enforce"`.
- CI (`.github/workflows/verification-gates.yml`): set the job's
  `continue-on-error` to `false` (or remove the line), then add the check to
  the branch's required status checks. Note `commit-on-main`/`block-stash` are
  hook-only — branch protection on the remote is the enforcement floor for the
  *default branch itself*.
- Re-running the scaffold NEVER overwrites your edits: re-install refuses on
  any existing artifact (there is no `--force`).

### Uninstall

```bash
bash <plugin>/skills/verification-scaffold/scripts/verification-scaffold.sh --target . --uninstall <guard>
```

removes only that guard's emitted files plus its `.claude/settings.json` hook
entry; shared artifacts (the workflow, `.gitleaks.toml` when another guard
still needs it) stay — the workflow is only edited when this guard's job block
is actually present. `--uninstall` on a never-installed guard is a no-op that
lists what is installed, and once no guard artifact remains this marker block
is pruned (a file that held only this block is removed).

### Requirements

- bash + POSIX tools (stock macOS included). Emitted hooks resolve `gitleaks`
  via `command -v` at exec time; the CI job uses the SHA-pinned
  `gitleaks/gitleaks-action`.
- The secret-scan hook needs `gitleaks` on PATH to run locally (8.24.x
  recommended); without it the hook warns and allows (advisory) — the CI job
  still scans every PR.
- `.claude/settings.json` hook entries serve Claude-Code-compatible agent
  sessions; the workflow is the floor for everyone else.
